OK help set -> Set or query the value of a openMSX setting or Tcl variable
  set <setting>          shows current value
  set <setting> <value>  set a new value
Use 'help set <setting>' to get more info on a specific
openMSX setting.

OK help type -> The type command is currently implemented by type_via_keyboard. (This can
be changed with the default_type_proc setting.) Here is the help of that
command:
Type a string in the emulated MSX.
Use -release to make sure the keys are always released before typing new ones (necessary for some game input routines, but in general, this means typing is twice as slow).
Use -freq to tweak how fast typing goes and how long the keys will be pressed (and released in case -release was used). Keys will be typed at the given frequency and will remain pressed/released for 1/freq seconds
Use -cancel to cancel a (long) in-progress type command.
